<title>NORWAY: Norway buys armaments from Rheinmetall.</title>
<headline>Norway buys armaments from Rheinmetall.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Norwegian Defence Ministry approved on Thursday a contract under which the state procurement office will buy 155 mm artillery shells worth 300 million crowns from Rheinmetall Industrie AG of Germany.</p>
<p>In return, Rheinmetall committed itself to buying ammunition components from Norwegian firms Raufoss Technology ASA, Dyno Industrier ASA and the Kongsberg Group AS for the same amount, a statement said.</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom +47 22 42 50 41</p>
</text>
